    "content": {
      "rendered": "<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-media-detail-hero nasa-gb-align-wide width-full maxw-full margin-y-5 desktop:margin-y-7 padding-x-3 media-detail-hero--suppress-inner-media-caption hds-module alignwide wp-block-nasa-blocks-media-detail-hero\">\t<div class=\"grid-container grid-container-block padding-x-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"label margin-bottom-1\">APOD</p>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"heading-22 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-2\">Astronomy Picture of the Day</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3 media-detail-hero__subtext\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer.\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"media-detail-hero__media margin-bottom-6\">\n\t\t\t\t<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-media hds-module wp-block-image\"><div class=\"margin-left-auto margin-right-auto nasa-block-align-full\"><div class=\"hds-media-wrapper margin-left-auto margin-right-auto\"><figure class=\"hds-media-inner hds-cover-wrapper hds-media-ratio-fit \"><a href=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=2048&#038;h=1542&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1542\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=1542&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"attachment-2048x2048 size-2048x2048\" alt=\"A dense globular cluster of stars.\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 50%; object-position: 50% 50%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=1542&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2048w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=300&amp;h=226&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=768&amp;h=578&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=771&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=1157&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=400&amp;h=301&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=600&amp;h=452&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=900&amp;h=678&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=904&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/NGC5139CadenasParra.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1506&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2048px) 100vw, 2048px\" /></a></figure></div></div></div>\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h1 class=\"display-48 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3\">Globular Cluster Omega Centauri</h1>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row media-detail-hero__content-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-0 media-detail-hero__description\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Explanation:</strong> Globular star cluster <a href=\"https://earthsky.org/clusters-nebulae-galaxies/omega-centauri-milky-ways-prize-star-cluster\" rel=\"noopener\">Omega Centauri</a> <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/fap/ap080906.html\" rel=\"noopener\">packs</a> about 10 million stars much older than the Sun into a volume some 150 light-years in diameter. Also known as NGC 5139, at a distance of 15,000 light-years it&#8217;s the largest and brightest of 200 or so known <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Globular_clusters\" rel=\"noopener\">globular clusters</a> that roam the halo of our Milky Way galaxy. Though most star clusters consist of stars with the same age and composition, the enigmatic Omega Cen exhibits the presence of <a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2021A%26A...653L...8L/abstract\" rel=\"noopener\">different</a> stellar populations with a spread of ages and chemical abundances. In fact, <a href=\"https://esahubble.org/news/heic0809/\" rel=\"noopener\">Omega Cen may be</a> the <a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2019NatAs...3..667I/abstract\" rel=\"noopener\">remnant</a> core of a small galaxy merging with the Milky Way. With a <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/fap/ap151224.html\" rel=\"noopener\">yellowish hue</a>, Omega Centauri&#8217;s red giant stars are easy to pick out in this sharp telescopic view. A two-decade-long exploration of the dense star cluster with the Hubble Space Telescope has revealed evidence for a massive black hole near the <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/hubble/nasas-hubble-finds-strong-evidence-for-intermediate-mass-black-hole-in-omega-centauri/\">center of Omega Centauri</a>.<br><br><strong>APOD&#8217;s email for image submissions has changed.</strong> Please see: <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/lib/apsubmit2015.html\" rel=\"noopener\">APOD Submissions</a>.<br><strong>APOD&#8217;s main NASA site is <a href=\"https://asterisk.apod.com/viewtopic.php?t=45023\" rel=\"noopener\">moving</a>:</strong> From <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/\" rel=\"noopener\">apod.nasa.gov</a> to <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod\">science.nasa.gov/apod</a><br><strong>Tomorrow&#8217;s picture: </strong>reflections on a starry night<br>\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"display-none desktop:display-block desktop:grid-col-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-5 margin-top-3 desktop:margin-top-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<table class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-table width-full\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tbody>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Date</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSeptember 25, 2026\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Credit &amp; Copyright:</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jcadenasparra/\" rel=\"noopener\">Javier O. Cadenas Parra</a>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Authors &amp; editors:</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tJerry Bonnell, Cecilia Chirenti, Robert Nemiroff, Keighley Rockcliffe\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">A service of:</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\